#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:5 579edc0695254acb902d2ca67b7cd256
msgid "Guided Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:7 3625397c8be940eaa77927fd6509c1f4
msgid ""
"Guided mode is a capability of Copter to dynamically guide the copter to "
"a target location wirelessly using a telemetry radio module and ground "
"station application. This page provides instructions for using guided "
"mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:12 af329ea0e0774bd8b0bee1e6ea2a0431
msgid ""
"Guided Mode can also be used by LUA scripts and companion computers to "
"command vehicle movement and navigation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:15 36c7e8fb220243c0804c78c18e641d42
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:17 9a7d0696c5fd446fba39e45a02d720c0
msgid ""
"Guided mode is not a traditional flight mode that would be assigned to a "
"mode switch like other flight modes. The guided mode capability is "
"enabled using a ground station application (such as Mission Planner) and "
"a :ref:`telemetry radio <common-telemetry-landingpage>`. This capability "
"allows the pilot to interactively command the copter to travel to a "
"target location by clicking on a point on the Mission Planner Flight Data"
" map. Once the location is reached, the copter will hover at that "
"location, waiting for the next target. Follow Me mode also uses Guided "
"Mode to make the copter follow the pilot around the field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:32 e369baec1d3e4dc1b3e3fbcdbed71b01
msgid "What you'll need"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:34 cac745794bab41cfa927e556312c911c
msgid ""
"To use guided mode, you'll need a :ref:`telemetry radio <common-"
"telemetry-landingpage>` allowing your computer and autopilot to "
"communicate during flight, a ground station computer or tablet, and a "
"ground station application such as :ref:`Mission Planner <planner:home>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:40 05775e88af244d91ad309d370658cf99
msgid "Instructions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:42 1238867d539149428e4066e9e0f5567b
msgid ""
"Set up your copter at the field and establish a MAVLink connection over "
"wireless telemetry between your copter and your laptop."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:44 b4bd0affbc4f403d90c96ba25e93bdb4
msgid ""
"On your laptop, using the software that came with the telemetry module, "
"make sure that it's working and that you have a GPS lock."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:46 991bbae1cdae40d49422dac36ef8cf93
msgid "Take off in :ref:`Loiter Mode <loiter-mode>` and climb to a safe altitude"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:47 c8239021e7a0466dba89836cd80bcc35
msgid ""
"In the Mission Planner Flight Data screen map, try right-clicking on a "
"nearby spot and select \"Fly to Here\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:49 9aaa1c634ea04a2e906403ee0f90aab0
msgid ""
"You will be asked for a guided mode altitude. Enter an above home "
"altitude in meters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:55 82db76b6b66e460083a7fd4751f15758
msgid ""
"A \"Guided\" target should appear on the map and the orange line (which "
"indicates the target heading) should point to this guided target."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:61 d7568212d8844168be289aff77389f2e
msgid ""
"The vehicle should fly to the target location and wait there until you "
"enter another location or switch to another mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:66 d83775e005af4d80ad43f71ea294a690
msgid ""
"On *Mission Planner* there is no need to set up one of your flight modes "
"as \"Guided\". This may not be the case for other Ground Control "
"Stations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:71 c00002df8711431881545bfb01684690
msgid "Speed Control"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:73 228a999f45ea4c49b9bcd60a09aa0236
msgid ""
"The maximum horizontal speed of the copter can be adjusted with the "
"**Speed** (:ref:`WPNAV_SPEED<WPNAV_SPEED>`) parameter from the Mission "
"Planner's Config/Tuning >> Copter Pids screen (see blue box above).  The "
"default is 1000 meaning 10m/s.  A typical copter can reach top speeds of "
"10m/s ~ 13m/s (i.e. 1000 ~ 1300) before it becomes unable to both "
"maintain altitude and horizontal speed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:80 1b7e08612f8a4b5182884c165cefcce7
msgid ""
"The vertical speeds up and down can similar be adjusted with the **Speed "
"Up** (:ref:`WPNAV_SPEED_UP<WPNAV_SPEED_UP>`) and **Speed Dn** "
"(:ref:`WPNAV_SPEED_DN<WPNAV_SPEED_DN>`) parameters. "
":ref:`WPNAV_ACCEL_Z<WPNAV_ACCEL_Z>` determines how fast the speed can "
"change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:82 b0c6c5b738af4b909024f8aae8774a3e
msgid ""
"Speed can also be controlled while in GUIDED mode with :ref:`MAVLink "
"commands <common-mavlink-mission-command-messages-mav_cmd>` like "
":ref:`DO_CHANGE_SPEED<mav_cmd_do_change_speed>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:85 07e372ae39f24d15b7ff580b2603fc47
msgid "Guided Mode Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:87 1519c53a4036415db70583948e9ffebc
msgid ""
"The :ref:`GUID_OPTIONS<GUID_OPTIONS>` parameter allows several guided "
"mode behavior changes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:90 e847e9cafa384055ba59651909e91d3c
msgid "Bit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:90 6239f5f75e2c45458eb2876087852d8b
msgid "Meaning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:92 cb75b8b09e694ab7a6a04e1b9d8eacb7
msgid "0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:92 a0fd296c08a44c00a561627a9e1089a2
msgid "Allow Arming from Transmitter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:93 1e072e38e2df42399c712daf6525e925
msgid "2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:93 706b58cf228048828a7457b161babfd1
msgid "Ignore pilot yaw input"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:94 2c0d5bd4cd124605b1da9bd61c632dc2
msgid "3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:94 df5937c6d1914924b064c57f4d005322
msgid "SetAttitudeTarget interprets Thrust As Thrust"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:95 be26583e83204b1ba2042b5bfc472096
msgid "4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:95 084a2f19477d4633bc7ac17b96342427
msgid "Do not stabilize PositionXY"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:96 005acba5be154f00a343a90cfff5a756
msgid "5"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:96 9b2e68f4264b49ab98c76681b479a815
msgid "Do not stabilize VelocityXY"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:97 6d092a7e4267440db641799af7667fc4
msgid "6"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:97 7d3a7bf98e64459da7237e08ad9086b3
msgid "Waypoint navigation used for position targets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:98 fed795146c9d485496e396baec7a207c
msgid "7"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:98 6d3bb8ca4009402f902d2297627d22a9
msgid "Allow weathervaning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:101 ed8e1f06b50c494d998668ef1fb6ba10
msgid "Bit 0 (e.g. \"1\") allowing arming in Guided mode from the RC transmitter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:103 a29fa9a1d2c64123bbf84d8b15b38dca
msgid ""
"Bit 2 (e.g. \"4\") disables the pilot's ability to change the vehicle's "
"heading using the RC transmitter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:105 3a2afd8845504f29bb6c7c81283b92d0
msgid ""
"Bit 3 (e.g. \"8\") changes the interpretation of the `SET_ATTITUDE_TARGET"
" MAVLink "
"<https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html#SET_ATTITUDE_TARGET>`__ "
"command's ``thrust`` field to be pure thrust expressed as a value between"
" 0 and 1, instead of a climb rate. See :ref:`Copter Commands in Guided "
"Mode <copter-commands-in-guided-mode>` for more details"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:107 2e2d38c701a642cf98659c2839627c0f
msgid ""
"Bit 4 (e.g. \"16\") disables the position controller's XY axis position "
"error correction.  This may be useful if an external controller is "
"providing high speed targets which already include position error "
"correction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:109 4458dfd08fab49608eb29ed64b079b62
msgid ""
"Bit 5 (e.g. \"32\") is the same as above but affects the position "
"controller's velocity error correction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:111 ddfcd8aa4f874a60a26db918405a9770
msgid ""
"Bit 6 (e.g. \"64\") enables S-Curve path planning (the same as is used in"
" :ref:`Auto mode <auto-mode>`) to reach the position target.  This may "
"result a smoother acceleration and deceleration but the position target "
"cannot be updated quickly.  This also allows :ref:`object avoidance path "
"planning <common-object-avoidance-landing-page>` (e.g. :ref:`Bendy Ruler "
"<common-oa-bendyruler>` and :ref:`Dijkstras<common-oa-dijkstras>`) to be "
"used in Guided mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:113 7f99a330a4e64cf4bf57a7036373f2e0
msgid "Bit 7 (e.g. \"128\") enables :ref:`weathervaning <weathervaning>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:115 76c6905efaea4b308ddf45312f84bcc7
msgid ""
"The :ref:`GUID_TIMEOUT<GUID_TIMEOUT>` parameter holds the timeout (in "
"seconds) when the vehicle is being controlled using attitude, velocity "
"and/or acceleration commands. If no commands are received from the "
"companion computer for this many seconds, the vehicle will slow to a stop"
" (if velocity and/or acceleration commands were being provided) or hold a"
" level hover (if attitude commands were provided). The default setting is"
" 3 seconds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:120 f9c0564f371343e58a38d268b6c8e37a
msgid "Guided_NoGPS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:121 b68440de043446cf85c0f0651642ed41
msgid ""
"This variation of Guided mode does not require a GPS but it only accepts "
"`attitude targets "
"<https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html#SET_ATTITUDE_TARGET>`__.  "
"Because it does not accept position or velocity targets like regular "
"Guided mode it is generally not useful for regular users.  This mode was "
"created for use by companion computers that may want to fly the vehicle "
"as if it was in AltHold mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:125 6b9e47d4746a4ef7aa139101cc831bd1
msgid ""
"Guided_NoGPS does not allow a vehicle to hold position without a GPS "
"(i.e. non-GPS navigation).  For information on :ref:`non-GPS navigation "
"see this wiki page <common-non-gps-navigation-landing-page>`"
msgstr ""

